counterfactuals.output:
1. A warehouse automation system comprising:

a plurality of racks defining a plurality of storage spaces arranged at a plurality of rack levels for storing items;

at least one picking aisle extending alongside the plurality of racks and providing travel access to the storage spaces;

a plurality of level decks disposed at respective elevations and communicating with the at least one picking aisle, each level deck being configured to support travel of a picking vehicle at a corresponding rack level; and

a control system configured to direct the picking vehicle along the at least one picking aisle and onto one or more of the level decks to access selected storage spaces,

wherein the storage spaces are arranged among the rack levels such that, during a common pass of the picking vehicle along the at least one picking aisle, the picking vehicle is enabled to perform a plurality of sequential picks from different storage spaces at different rack levels without returning to a starting location between the sequential picks.
